<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee to continue to see mild temps - Somar.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee to continue to see mild temps - Somar.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's coffee regions will continue to see mild temperatures throughout this week with no threatening polar air mass forecast to enter coffee areas in the seven-day outlook, local meteorologists Somar said Sunday.</p>
<p>Minimum temperatures over the weekend were above 10 degrees Celsius, said Somar forecaster Marcos Massari.</p>
<p>&quot;No change is expected in the next seven days,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>A weak cold front will quickly pass through coffee regions from July 14 bringing scattered showers but otherwise the forecast was for sunshine throughout the remainder of the week, he said.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
